-- `crm_done` backfill: a `sending` row gets 2 (a put may have started; the safe path decides); a row whose `last_error` is `refused`, `unreachable`, `ambiguous` or `crash_while_sending` (the error came from the send, so the CRM was asked first) gets 1, in any state; a row whose `last_error` is `internal:CrmNothingStored`, `internal:KeyError`, `internal:ValueError` or `internal:LookupError` (the error happened before the CRM put) keeps 0, so the next try asks the CRM; any other `internal:` error gets 2; a `failed` row with a label and any other error gets 1 (older books asked the CRM before the first send); any other row that was tried (attempts > 0) gets 2. A row never tried (attempts 0, not `sending`) and a `sent` row are never touched. The order is the order of this list (`test_backfill_classes` checks nine of these cases).
